                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "17d510d7-d5e5-3c5c-a4fb-ed4c81fe85b2",
                        "entry_id": "1e810f52-3a8c-33ae-be26-5c762c2fe22c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To remove or separate the lining from."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3b334e8-ca32-4303-863e-087ba4f7ab7f",
                                "sense_id": "17d510d7-d5e5-3c5c-a4fb-ed4c81fe85b2",
                                "text": "as in the case of gout, a disease of the sufferer's own making, from excess of de-electrising food and drink, which uncoats and unlines the nerves, and thus leaves the nervous fluid, from casual circumstances, to almost lacerate the brain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f10efd2-c4bf-4551-948e-8190267bc721",
                                "sense_id": "17d510d7-d5e5-3c5c-a4fb-ed4c81fe85b2",
                                "text": "No more that unenquiring heart Perused the sweet home of her breast, Than turtle-doves unline their nest To scan the outer part."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2983eecb-e7f4-4c49-92b0-f4ded3d27af1",
                                "sense_id": "17d510d7-d5e5-3c5c-a4fb-ed4c81fe85b2",
                                "text": "These instruments are so produced as to suit the procedure of vivification by unlining, which is the one that I exclusively employ ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8caf8d90-9ea5-32b1-8f2e-633f0a7083fa",
                        "entry_id": "1e810f52-3a8c-33ae-be26-5c762c2fe22c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To undergo a (now debunked) process in which the tissue of a plant separates into identical layers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "82b4795e-8c94-4be7-a5d2-b13416bb8232",
                                "sense_id": "8caf8d90-9ea5-32b1-8f2e-633f0a7083fa",
                                "text": "There is no instance of unlining which may not be as well explained by the theory of alternation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cd9cd36-14fe-4415-b55f-559c5e2764fa",
                                "sense_id": "8caf8d90-9ea5-32b1-8f2e-633f0a7083fa",
                                "text": "The name dédoublement of Duval, which has been translated deduplication, literally means unlining'; the original hypothesis being, that the organs in question unline, or tend to separate into two or more layers, each having the same structure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0f4949e-578b-4c84-9cd3-f928a1dc4636",
                                "sense_id": "8caf8d90-9ea5-32b1-8f2e-633f0a7083fa",
                                "text": "The carpophore unlines itself at maturity, and the vittæ are wide and solitary in each furrow."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d19e4a37-d411-30f2-a8a5-e0bf7324bfc5",
                        "entry_id": "1e810f52-3a8c-33ae-be26-5c762c2fe22c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To empty (a purse)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "00eeea9e-6f24-40fd-a4f5-c2b1811032c2",
                                "sense_id": "d19e4a37-d411-30f2-a8a5-e0bf7324bfc5",
                                "text": "I'll live by a pittance. Unline my purse, and use my person, and for my limbs, take the best in the bunch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19979124-73d0-4215-b7d5-3c50297ab6c7",
                                "sense_id": "d19e4a37-d411-30f2-a8a5-e0bf7324bfc5",
                                "text": "How many old, Decrepit packs of eighty do we see Get wives, that first unline their purse, then out, Like skinless rats, drive their lean carcasses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c0bfd56-1386-4a0b-9f7d-932ffb1e35f2",
                                "sense_id": "d19e4a37-d411-30f2-a8a5-e0bf7324bfc5",
                                "text": "As now rich Opportunity doth give to make you Fame-full though it empt your Pouche: Two Kings thus met, make Kingdomes richly thrive, though it unlines their Purse with wearing much: Then, sith but seld, or ne're Kings consort thus, Be glorious now, or still inglorious."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cef0aff6-c37b-369a-b6f7-9939341dcf5b",
                        "entry_id": "1e810f52-3a8c-33ae-be26-5c762c2fe22c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take out of (literal or figurative) alignment; to disconnect."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8671348a-809e-434b-ac37-4b60bb5edca4",
                                "sense_id": "cef0aff6-c37b-369a-b6f7-9939341dcf5b",
                                "text": "To-morrow doth Luxurio promise me He will unline himself from bitchery ;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d63c14c-9ac3-4878-b20d-501e2e437047",
                                "sense_id": "cef0aff6-c37b-369a-b6f7-9939341dcf5b",
                                "text": "When the eccentric lowers the pitman, it unlines the toggles and the swing jaw is free to recede from the fixed jaw ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf1e9969-f602-4e9e-adca-8565595cc393",
                                "sense_id": "cef0aff6-c37b-369a-b6f7-9939341dcf5b",
                                "text": "And as I've been walking, sure enough, I see little white dots on the hills, those little sheep, and I can see cattle lined up and then unlining about a mile off on the plains ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22cb25e7-ad47-3c7b-9048-186ff61d82dc",
                        "entry_id": "1e810f52-3a8c-33ae-be26-5c762c2fe22c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To remove or destroy one or more lines."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce87b4ad-8941-4a4b-937b-93d4e228fedc",
                                "sense_id": "22cb25e7-ad47-3c7b-9048-186ff61d82dc",
                                "text": "However, I am a Line, and they can't \"unline\" me very well. My soil is not good enough for a market-garden, and if it were, the surrounding inhabitants are too sparse to require so large a supply of the vegetable world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01b2bad8-0b89-475d-b6c2-460f3b3d1d7c",
                                "sense_id": "22cb25e7-ad47-3c7b-9048-186ff61d82dc",
                                "text": "She will ask herself whether the confined and relative reason of the artist can be deemed superior to the infinite, absolute reason of the Creator; whether it is for man to rectify God; whether mutilation can improve the beauty of nature; whether are be authorised to unline—if we may use the word — man, life, creation; . . . . whether, in fine, incompleteness be an element of harmony?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0983db2-34dd-4fd9-983f-2115151000a2",
                                "sense_id": "22cb25e7-ad47-3c7b-9048-186ff61d82dc",
                                "text": "Maxwell cars are of unit construction that no stress can unline."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
